From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 09:48:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] fix(status): legacy producers are explicit unknown;
 failed roster keeps asks; null fence parity

Review t_01a1cea80dbe0cc1 findings 4, 7 and 8 (desktop/sidebar).
- 4: a failed roster source keeps each cached record as an explicit unknown under its own
  identity, so retained human requests still count as outstanding.
- 7: TS project() treats a null expected identity as "no fence", like Python's
  `expected_identity is not None`; shared golden case null-expected-identity-is-no-fence.
- 8: a sidebar row with live (unparked) card counts but no execution_observations array
  (older producer) adds explicit unknown instead of reading as certain work. Parked waits
  keep their legacy wait; a current producer's array decides on its own.

RED: the new vitest cases fail at b529083fbd. GREEN: 10 targeted vitest files 689 passed;
7 targeted Python files 420 passed; tsc clean; scripts/check --only health ok.
